.Dd June 25, 2026
.Dt CAN 4
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm CAN
.Nd Controller Area Network protocol family
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Cd "options CAN"
.Pp
.In netcan/can.h
.In netcan/can/raw.h
.Ft int
.Fn socket AF_CAN SOCK_RAW CAN_RAW
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
protocol family provides access to the Controller Area Network (CAN) bus
through the socket interface, in a way that is source-compatible with the
Linux SocketCAN API.
A CAN frame is exchanged as a whole datagram rather than a byte stream.
.Pp
A raw CAN socket is created with
.Fn socket AF_CAN SOCK_RAW CAN_RAW .
It is bound to a CAN network interface with
.Xr bind 2
using a
.Vt struct sockaddr_can :
.Bd -literal -offset indent
struct sockaddr_can {
	uint8_t		can_len;	/* sizeof(struct sockaddr_can) */
	sa_family_t	can_family;	/* AF_CAN */
	int		can_ifindex;	/* interface index, 0 = all */
	/* protocol-specific address information */
};
.Ed
.Pp
A
.Va can_ifindex
of zero binds to every CAN interface.
After a successful
.Xr bind 2
the socket may be used with
.Xr read 2
and
.Xr write 2 ,
or with
.Xr recvfrom 2
and
.Xr sendto 2
to receive or specify the interface explicitly.
.Pp
Frames are described by
.Vt struct can_frame
(classic CAN, up to 8 data bytes) or
.Vt struct canfd_frame
(CAN FD, up to 64 data bytes); both begin with a 32-bit
.Va can_id
that carries the identifier and the
.Dv CAN_EFF_FLAG ,
.Dv CAN_RTR_FLAG
and
.Dv CAN_ERR_FLAG
flag bits.
.Sh SOCKET OPTIONS
Raw CAN sockets support the following options at level
.Dv SOL_CAN_RAW ,
set and retrieved with
.Xr setsockopt 2
and
.Xr getsockopt 2 .
.Bl -tag -width CAN_RAW_RECV_OWN_MSGS
.It Dv CAN_RAW_FILTER
.Pq array of Vt struct can_filter
Set the receive filter.
A frame is accepted when
.Va "(can_id & can_mask) == (filter.can_id & can_mask)"
for any of the configured filters.
The match is inverted for a filter whose
.Va can_id
has
.Dv CAN_INV_FILTER
set.
The default is a single match-all filter; an empty array receives nothing.
.It Dv CAN_RAW_ERR_FILTER
.Pq Vt can_err_mask_t
Select which error message frames are received.
.It Dv CAN_RAW_LOOPBACK
.Pq Vt int , default on
Control whether locally sent frames are looped back to other sockets.
.It Dv CAN_RAW_RECV_OWN_MSGS
.Pq Vt int , default off
Control whether a socket receives the frames it sent itself.
.It Dv CAN_RAW_JOIN_FILTERS
.Pq Vt int , default off
Require all filters to match instead of any.
.It Dv CAN_RAW_FD_FRAMES
.Pq Vt int , default off
Allow CAN FD frames to be sent and received on the socket.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr socket 2 ,
.Xr slcan 4 ,
.Xr vcan 4 ,
.Xr slcand 8
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm
protocol family first appeared in
.Fx 16.0 .
It is derived from the
.Nx
.Pa sys/netcan
implementation and follows the Linux SocketCAN application interface.
